# Code style — TS + JSDoc, DRY, constants, Vue files

TypeScript is the type system. JSDoc documents **what** a public API does. Do not mix the two.

## Vue SFC order

In every `.vue` file, write blocks in this order:

1. `<template>`
2. `<script setup lang="ts">`

Do **not** put `<style>` in Vue files.

```vue
<!-- BAD — script before template, or <style> in the SFC -->
<script setup lang="ts">...</script>
<template>...</template>
<style scoped>...</style>

<!-- GOOD -->
<template>...</template>
<script setup lang="ts">
import '@/styles/views/landing.css'
</script>
```

## Styles — external CSS only

Move all component/page styles out of Vue SFCs into CSS files under `src/styles/`.

| Kind | Path | Name |
|---|---|---|
| View / page | `src/styles/views/` | Match the route name from `ROUTE_NAMES` (e.g. `landing`, `login`, `add-meal`) → `landing.css` |
| Component | `src/styles/components/` | Kebab-case of the component file (e.g. `LandingTopBar.vue` → `landing-top-bar.css`) |

Import the CSS from the matching Vue `<script setup>`. Prefer BEM / unique class prefixes (no Vue `scoped` needed). Replace former `:deep(...)` with a normal descendant selector.

Shared tokens and resets stay in `src/styles/base.css` and `src/styles/themes/`.

## No inline comments

No `//` comments, TODOs, or narrating code. Names explain locals and steps.

## JSDoc — required on public API

Add `/** */` on every **exported** function, composable, store, type, and constant module export.

- One short English sentence: what it does, not how
- Do **not** repeat types (`@param {string}`, `@returns {number}`, `@type`)
- Use `@param` / `@returns` only when the name is not enough (units, range, side effects)

Do not JSDoc trivial locals, private helpers, or Vue template markup.

## TypeScript

- Strict types on public signatures; no `any` unless asked
- Shared shapes live in `src/types/`, not inline in three files
- Prefer `type` / `interface` over JSDoc `@typedef`

## Do not repeat logic — extract it

Same calculation, mapping, guard, or navigation twice → extract.

- Vue logic → `src/composables/`
- Pure functions → `src/utils/`
- Shared UI → `src/components/common/`

Do not copy-paste a composable/query/store "with small tweaks". Extend the existing one.

## Do not hardcode — use constants

Magic numbers, enum-like strings, route names, URLs, limits, debounce ms, meal types, MIME lists, max file size, UI variant unions → `src/constants/` by domain (`routes.ts`, `ui.ts`, `meals.ts`, `api.ts`, `storage.ts`).

Copy → i18n. Colors → theme CSS variables. Import constants; never inline the same literal twice. Prefer reusing existing constants over adding a parallel string.
